From edb08e1565e3f7f6889751bd2a8c581715cd81de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Gorbachenko <alex.gorbachenko@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 31 May 2026 08:33:02 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Use jemalloc instead of system allocator
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the default system allocator with jemalloc via the
jemallocator crate.  Jemalloc uses per-thread arenas, eliminating
allocator lock contention when multiple threads allocate under load.

On musl targets (Alpine Linux, RouterOS containers, embedded systems),
the musl malloc global lock becomes the bottleneck.  At 40 Mbps on a
hAP ax³ (Cortex-A53): 67% CPU → 47% CPU (-20 p.p.).

Jemalloc is excluded from Windows (no C cross-compiler), MIPS/mips64
(__popcountdi2 missing), and armv7/armhf (__ffsdi2 missing).
Controlled via target-gated deps in Cargo.toml and #[cfg] in main.rs.
